Q: How to start ordered list from 2 not 1 with W3C validity and IE 6 compatibility? A: <p>This can be done via HTML directly with the <code>start</code> attribute</p>
<pre><code>&lt;ol start=&quot;2&quot;&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;item two&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;item three&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>It is <a href="http://www.highdots.com/forums/cascading-style-sheets/using-css-set-start-number-262555.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">not possible</a> with CSS only, and it seems like IE doesn't support the <code>start</code> attribute …</p>

Q: CodeIgniter query builder method is ignored when called after get() A: <p>It should be in this format</p>

<pre><code>$this-&gt;db-&gt;where("tablename.column", $task_id);
$this-&gt;db-&gt;order_by('tablename.column', 'ASC'); // or 'DESC'
$this-&gt;db-&gt;from('table');
</code></pre>
